{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":44.20000076293945,"text":"When Athens took on the Olympic Games of 2004, the football would not fit into one city. The matches were spread across five stadiums around the country, and one of them was here. The Pancreatio was built for exactly that and holds about 26,000 people. It has a running track around the pitch, so the stands sit further back than in a football-only ground, and it is used for athletics and concerts, too. The interesting question about a building like this is not how it was built, but what happened next. Many Olympic stadiums around the world emptied out once the games ended. This one did not. Cretan clubs play here, and it fills up regularly. A stadium only stays alive if somebody needs it on the Monday after the party.","words":[{"word":"When","start":0,"end":0.46000000834465027},{"word":"Athens","start":0.46000000834465027,"end":0.9200000166893005},{"word":"took","start":0.9200000166893005,"end":1.2599999904632568},{"word":"on","start":1.2599999904632568,"end":1.5},{"word":"the","start":1.5,"end":1.6799999475479126},{"word":"Olympic","start":1.6799999475479126,"end":2.0399999618530273},{"word":"Games","start":2.0399999618530273,"end":2.4200000762939453},{"word":"of","start":2.4200000762939453,"end":2.6600000858306885},{"word":"2004","start":2.6600000858306885,"end":3.440000057220459},{"word":"the","start":4,"end":4.139999866485596},{"word":"football","start":4.139999866485596,"end":4.460000038146973},{"word":"would","start":4.460000038146973,"end":4.739999771118164},{"word":"not","start":4.739999771118164,"end":5.039999961853027},{"word":"fit","start":5.039999961853027,"end":5.320000171661377},{"word":"into","start":5.320000171661377,"end":5.519999980926514},{"word":"one","start":5.519999980926514,"end":5.840000152587891},{"word":"city","start":5.840000152587891,"end":6.059999942779541},{"word":"The","start":6.619999885559082,"end":6.880000114440918},{"word":"matches","start":6.88000011444